).</p>
  <p><strong>Revision gate.</strong> Did the round shift the centre? Confirming: Rashi's dew note and Van de Giessen's tsur-concentration strengthen Source+Trajectory and the dew-echo to Hosea, without collapsing it to Source alone.</p>

  <h2>§5 Direction test as horizon</h2>
  <p>🔵 Confessional. Matthew 18:21–35 continues Ha'azinu's forgetting-line from the other side: the servant forgiven an immeasurable debt who seizes his fellow by the throat is Jeshurun who forgot the Rock — the forgetting becomes visible in the hard hand. “From Me is your fruit found” (Hos.): the fruit of received grace is grace passed on. 🔴 Guarded: Matt. 18 does not determine the peshat of Deut. 32; it is horizon. And “seventy times seven” is no new counting but the end of counting — as the Rock stops counting against the one who returns.</p>

  <h2>§6 Status table</h2>
  <table>
  <tr><th>Claim</th><th>Status</th></tr>
  <tr><td>The Rock (tsur) is the Godname of the song; idols are no rock (32:4,15,18,31)</td><td>🟢 load-bearing</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Abundance, not wilderness, becomes the test; forgetting = living as if the Giver were not needed (32:15–18)</td><td>🟢 load-bearing</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Heaven/earth as eternal and rewarding/punishing witnesses; dew note (Rashi, Sifrei 306)</td><td>🟢 load-bearing (verified)</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Ba'at only here + 1 Sam. 2:29; shayah hapax (Van de Giessen)</td><td>🟢/🟡 pre-peshat</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Moses–Isaiah code-switch (Tanchuma)</td><td>🟡 suggestive (aggada)</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Reflex-landing on receiving/surrender as endpoint; sentimental “letting go”</td><td>🔴 guardrail</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Matt. 18: forgetting/returning visible in treatment of the neighbour; the dew-echo (32:2 ↔ Hos. 14:5)</td><td>🔵 confessional</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Onkelos/Ibn Ezra/Ramban on 32:4/32:15</td><td>⚪ open verification point</td></tr>
  </table>

  <h2>§7 Podcast rendering</h2>
  <p>One physical image carries the landing: the field that cannot compel rain. The farmer can plough, sow, fertilise — but he cannot command the sky; the rain comes toward him. So is the Word: gift, not production. And the second half of the image: what grows on your field, you hand out — the fruit of received rain is not a store to lock away but a harvest to pass on.</p>

  <h2>§8 Source accountability</h2>
  <p>Van de Giessen, Notes on Deuteronomy (18–34): tsur (32:4,15,18,31), Jeshurun + ba'at (32:15; cf. 1 Sam. 2:29), shayah hapax and “begets/bears” (32:18), setumot/column layout — verified from the file. Rashi on 32:1 (Sifrei Devarim 306) and the two-witnesses (Deut. 19:15) — verified via Sefaria. Tanchuma Ha'azinu 2 🟡. Onkelos/Ibn Ezra/Ramban: still to be verified. Name: Yeshua. Author: Arie Alberts.</p>
